Rebuild in the Boson AI blog visual system, with the poster's own figures

Design now follows boson.ai/blog/ihbench: committed dark theme, Manrope
display over Plus Jakarta Sans body, green accent, 820px reading column,
pill links, stat tiles, and the same leaderboard table treatment.

Figures are no longer recreated. Every graphic the poster labels a Figure
is now the poster's own artwork, rendered straight from the PDF:

- Figures 1-3 extracted as embedded raster images.
- Figures 4-8 and the scenario breakdown rendered from the PDF's vector
  drawing with PyMuPDF, cropped on text anchors. These had previously
  been flattened into HTML tables, which lost the charts entirely.

Table 1 stays an HTML table: the poster calls it a table, not a figure,
and it needs to stay selectable and scrollable on a phone.

